{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And after that, his brother came out, etc.</b> I heard from a certain expositor, according to its plain sense: it was fitting for him to hold him to restrain him. Jacob was formed from the first drop and Esau from the second. Go and learn from a tube whose mouth is short: give it two stones one after the other — the one that enters first comes out last, and the one that enters last comes out first. Thus Esau, who was formed from the last, came out first, and Jacob, who was formed first, came out last. And Jacob came to restrain him — that he should be first for birth as he was first for formation, and would release his mother's womb and take the birthright by right." "<b>By the heel of Esau.</b> A sign that this one is not adequate to finish his kingship until this one stands and takes it from him." "<b>And he called his name Jacob.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He. Another matter: his father called him Jacob on account of the holding of the heel." "<b>Sixty years old.</b> Ten years from when he married her until she became thirteen years old and fit for pregnancy — and these ten years he waited for her, as his father did for Sarah. Once she did not conceive, he knew she was barren, and prayed for her (Yevamot 64), and a maidservant he did not wish to take, because he had been sanctified on Mount Moriah to be a perfect burnt-offering."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:33.604316568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}